    "type": "post",
    "title": "FINAL MEME THREAD!",
    "content": "<document version=\"2.0\"><paragraph>Congratulations to everyone for finishing the final exam! It was a challenging exam, and we’re proud of all of y’all for pushing through it. As a celebration of the end of the final exam, we’re reviving an old CS 70 tradition and bringing it to EECS 182: THE FINAL MEME THREAD. Please use this thread to post your memes about EECS 182!!!!!<break/><break/><bold>A quick but important note, that these memes and any comments on memes must be respectful, so no memes / comments that degrade or put down any students / staff.</bold> <bold>This also includes the common “male gaze” meme (where a man and a woman are walking, and the man is looking at another woman behind him with a smug look on his face). I will be monitoring this thread closely, and redacting any memes that are disrespectful in nature.</bold></paragraph><paragraph>As a source of inspiration, here are some memes that have brought some laughs in the past! </paragraph><figure><image src=\"https://static.us.edusercontent.com/files/kpigOUimX8Lb0PmnVGseDaPw\" width=\"658\" height=\"486.4325925925926\"/></figure><figure><image src=\"https://static.us.edusercontent.com/files/gEvKxdb2Gr3btyhdq4Yibvfk\" width=\"500\" height=\"701\"/></figure><figure><image src=\"https://static.us.edusercontent.com/files/0CKAAjdPO1uPOEGaFPc4n0VF\" width=\"658\" height=\"206.9182389937107\"/></figure><paragraph>We're excited to see your memes below! Who knows? Maybe we'll use them somewhere the next time this class is taught again.</paragraph></document>",
    "document": "Congratulations to everyone for finishing the final exam! It was a challenging exam, and we’re proud of all of y’all for pushing through it. As a celebration of the end of the final exam, we’re reviving an old CS 70 tradition and bringing it to EECS 182: THE FINAL MEME THREAD. Please use this thread to post your memes about EECS 182!!!!!\n\nA quick but important note, that these memes and any comments on memes must be respectful, so no memes / comments that degrade or put down any students / staff. This also includes the common “male gaze” meme (where a man and a woman are walking, and the man is looking at another woman behind him with a smug look on his face). I will be monitoring this thread closely, and redacting any memes that are disrespectful in nature.\n\nAs a source of inspiration, here are some memes that have brought some laughs in the past! \n\nWe're excited to see your memes below! Who knows? Maybe we'll use them somewhere the next time this class is taught again.",
